Certainly! Implementing real-time synchronization using WebSockets involves setting up a WebSocket server, handling client connections, and ensuring data consistency and handling disconnections. Here's a comprehensive guide to help you implement the `NetworkSync` component:

### Step 1: Set Up WebSocket Server

First, set up the WebSocket server and handle client connections, disconnections, and messages.

### Step 2: Handle Real-Time Synchronization

Implement logic to synchronize data between clients and the server. This includes handling disconnections and ensuring data consistency.

### Step 3: Manage Client Connections

Maintain a list of connected clients and broadcast messages to all connected clients.

### Example Implementation

Here's an example implementation of the `NetworkSync` component:

```typescript
import WebSocket from 'ws';

class NetworkSync {
  private webSocketServer: WebSocket.Server;
  private clients: Set<WebSocket> = new Set();

  constructor() {
    this.webSocketServer = new WebSocket.Server({ port: 8080 });
    this.setupListeners();
  }

  private setupListeners() {
    this.webSocketServer.on('connection', (socket: WebSocket) => {
      console.log('Client connected');
      this.clients.add(socket);

      socket.on('message', (data: string) => {
        this.handleMessage(data, socket);
      });

      socket.on('close', () => {
        console.log('Client disconnected');
        this.clients.delete(socket);
      });

      socket.on('error', (error: Error) => {
        console.error('WebSocket error:', error);
        this.clients.delete(socket);
      });
    });
  }

  private handleMessage(data: string, socket: WebSocket) {
    try {
      const message = JSON.parse(data);
      this.broadcast(message, socket);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error parsing message:', error);
    }
  }

  private broadcast(message: any, sender: WebSocket) {
    this.clients.forEach(client => {
      if (client !== sender && client.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
        client.send(JSON.stringify(message));
      }
    });
  }

  public sendToAll(message: any) {
    this.clients.forEach(client => {
      if (client.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
        client.send(JSON.stringify(message));
      }
    });
  }
}

// Usage example
const networkSync = new NetworkSync();

// Example of sending a message to all clients
networkSync.sendToAll({ type: 'update', data: { x: 10, y: 20 } });
```

### Key Points

1. **WebSocket Server Initialization**: Set up the WebSocket server on a specified port.
2. **Connection Handling**: Listen for client connections and add them to the `clients` set.
