### Example: Sending a Message to a Specific Client

If you need to send a message to a specific client, you can use the `to` method:

```javascript
socket.on('private message', (data) => {
  console.log('private message:', data);
  socket.to(data.targetSocketId).emit('private message', data.message);
});
```

### Step 4: Testing with Multiple Clients

To test with multiple clients, open multiple browser tabs or use different devices to connect to the server. Each client should be able to send and receive messages independently.

### Summary

By following these steps, you can handle multiple clients connecting to your WebSocket server using Socket.IO. The server will manage connections and broadcasts efficiently, ensuring that all clients can communicate in real time.

