  console.log('Tokens:', tokens);
}).catch((error) => {
  console.error('Login error:', error);
});

logout().then((response) => {
  console.log('Logout response:', response);
}).catch((error) => {
  console.error('Logout error:', error);
});
```

### Conclusion

By following these steps, you can build a secure authentication system using JWT tokens with RS256 signing, integrated with Redis for session management. This setup ensures that your authentication system is secure and can handle a large number of concurrent requests. It also ensures compatibility with Redis for session caching and game state snapshots.

