### Basic Matchmaking Algorithm

The algorithm will:
1. Sort players by skill level.
2. Pair players with similar skill levels.
3. Return the matched pairs.

### Example Implementation

Here's a complete example of how you can implement and use a basic matchmaking algorithm in Node.js:

```javascript
const matchmaking = (players) => {
  // Sort players by skill level
  players.sort((a, b) => a.skillLevel - b.skillLevel);

  // Initialize an array to hold the matched pairs
  const matches = [];

  // Iterate through the sorted list of players and pair them
  for (let i = 0; i < players.length - 1; i += 2) {
    matches.push([players[i], players[i + 1]]);
  }

  return matches;
};

