Handling WebSocket reconnections is crucial to ensure that your application remains robust and reliable, especially in environments where network connectivity can be unstable. Here's a step-by-step guide on how to handle WebSocket reconnections in your React frontend.

### Step 1: Set Up WebSocket Connection

First, set up the WebSocket connection and handle reconnections. You can use the `socket.io-client` library to manage WebSocket connections.

