If your application needs to support multiple health check endpoints for different services, you can create distinct endpoints for each service. This allows you to provide granular health checks and readiness probes for each component of your application.

### Example Implementation

Let's assume you have two services within your application: `MatchmakingService` and `PlayerService`. Each service will have its own health and readiness endpoints.

#### Example in Java (Spring Boot)

Define separate health and readiness endpoints for each service.

```java
@RestController
