docker build -t your-docker-repo/player-service:latest -f Dockerfile.player .
docker push your-docker-repo/player-service:latest
```

### Step 4: Apply the Kubernetes Manifests

Apply the Kubernetes manifests to deploy your services:

```sh
kubectl apply -f matchmaking-deployment.yaml
kubectl apply -f player-deployment.yaml
```

### Conclusion

By defining distinct health and readiness endpoints for each service within your application, you can provide granular health checks and readiness probes. This setup helps ensure that each component of your application is monitored and managed effectively, contributing to the overall reliability and availability of your system.

