docker exec -it rabbitmq1 rabbitmqctl join_cluster rabbit@rabbitmq2

# Connect to the second node and add the third node
docker exec -it rabbitmq2 rabbitmqctl join_cluster rabbit@rabbitmq3
```

### Step 3: Configure Durable Exchanges and Queues

Ensure that your exchanges and queues are durable to survive restarts and network disruptions.

#### Example Node.js Code

```javascript
const amqp = require('amqplib');

async function setupRabbitMQ() {
  const connection = await amqp.connect('amqp://admin:admin@rabbitmq1:5672');
  const channel = await connection.createChannel();

  // Declare the exchange
  await channel.assertExchange('matchmaking-exchange', 'direct', { durable: true });

  // Declare the queue
  await channel.assertQueue('matchmaking-queue', { durable: true });

  // Bind the queue to the exchange
  await channel.bindQueue('matchmaking-queue', 'matchmaking-exchange', 'matchmaking-routing-key');

  console.log('RabbitMQ setup complete');
}

setupRabbitMQ().catch(console.error);
```

### Step 4: Implement Reconnection Logic in Clients

Ensure that your clients can reconnect to RabbitMQ after a network disruption. Use a retry mechanism with exponential backoff.

#### Example Node.js Code

```javascript
const amqp = require('amqplib');
const { delay } = require('./utils'); // Utility function for delay

async function connectToRabbitMQ() {
  let retries = 0;
  while (true) {
    try {
      const connection = await amqp.connect('amqp://admin:admin@rabbitmq1:5672');
      const channel = await connection.createChannel();

      // Declare the exchange
      await channel.assertExchange('matchmaking-exchange', 'direct', { durable: true });

      // Declare the queue
      await channel.assertQueue('matchmaking-queue', { durable: true });

      // Bind the queue to the exchange
      await channel.bindQueue('matchmaking-queue', 'matchmaking-exchange', 'matchmaking-routing-key');

      console.log('Connected to RabbitMQ');
      return { connection, channel };
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(`Failed to connect to RabbitMQ. Retrying... (${retries})`);
      await delay(Math.pow(2, retries++) * 100); // Exponential backoff
    }
  }
}

async function consumeMessage() {
  const { connection, channel } = await connectToRabbitMQ();

  channel.consume('matchmaking-queue', (msg) => {
    if (msg !== null) {
      console.log('Received message:', JSON.parse(msg.content.toString()));
      channel.ack(msg);
    }
  }, { noAck: false });

  console.log('Waiting for messages...');
}

consumeMessage().catch(console.error);
```

### Step . Monitor and Maintain

Regularly monitor the health of your RabbitMQ cluster and ensure that all nodes are up and communicating correctly. Use the management interface to check the status of nodes, exchanges, and queues.

### Conclusion

By setting up a RabbitMQ cluster, configuring durable exchanges and queues, and implementing robust reconnection logic in your clients, you can ensure that your RabbitMQ setup is resilient against network disruptions. Regular monitoring and maintenance will help you maintain a reliable messaging system.

