  console.log('PC2 ICE candidate:', candidate);
  pc1.addIceCandidate(candidate);
});

pc1.on('message', (data) => {
  console.log('PC1 Received message:', data);
});

pc2.on('message', (data) => {
  console.log('PC2 Received message:', data);
});
```

### Conclusion

By following these steps, you should be able to establish a peer-to-peer connection using WebRTC data channels in your React Native app. If you continue to experience issues, ensure that all configurations and event handlers are correctly implemented and that you have proper logging to track the connection process.

