Managing multiple components with different event listeners can be challenging, but there are several strategies to handle this effectively. One common approach is to use a centralized event manager or a context to manage event subscriptions and emissions. This way, you can ensure that event listeners are properly registered and cleaned up when components mount and unmount.

### Centralized Event Manager

A centralized event manager can help you manage multiple event listeners across different components. Here's an example of how you can implement this:

#### EventManager.js
```javascript
class EventManager {
  constructor() {
    this.listeners = {};
  }

  subscribe(eventName, callback) {
    if (!this.listeners[eventName]) {
      this.listeners[eventName] = new Set();
    }
    this.listeners[eventName].add(callback);
  }

  unsubscribe(eventName, callback) {
    if (this.listeners[eventName]) {
      this.listeners[eventName].delete(callback);
    }
  }

  emit(eventName, data) {
    if (this.listeners[eventName]) {
      this.listeners[eventName].forEach((callback) => {
        callback(data);
      });
    }
  }
}

export default new EventManager();
```

#### Usage in Components

Now, you can use this `EventManager` in your components to subscribe and unsubscribe from events.

#### ComponentA.js
