    };
  }, [subscribe, unsubscribe]);

  return (
    <View>
      <Text>Component B</Text>
    </View>
  );
};

export default ComponentB;
```

### Summary

By using a centralized event manager or context, you can effectively manage multiple event listeners across different components. This approach ensures that event listeners are properly registered and cleaned up, preventing memory leaks and making your code more maintainable.

How can I implement biometric login using React Native Biometrics 2.1.0 on supported devices, and what are the security considerations I should keep in mind? 
