### 1. Use Transactions for Atomicity
If you want to ensure that all updates are applied atomically, you can use Redis transactions. This ensures that either all updates succeed or none do, which can be important for maintaining data integrity.

### 2. Use `zadd` with Multiple Entries
Instead of calling `zadd` for each leader individually, you can pass multiple entries in a single call to `zadd`. This reduces the number of commands and network calls.

